BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Dog: A Human Pup Educational and Play Event
DTSTART:20260816T120500
DTEND:20260816T120500
UID:bf6cc65cfbc67b72ad2d92c7e624bd61@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:An inclusive\, queer-centric 19+ event for pet players and the
  curious with classes\, socializing\, activities\, and play! Get your tail
 s wagging and fill those treat bags for a day of puppy play! The vibe is 
 “dog park\, learning\, and tea” - if you’ve ever wondered if the hum
 an pup life is for you\, or if you’re already into it and want to sink d
 eeper into your headspace\, this is your time to explore. We’ll begin wi
 th two classes designed to help you understand and express your inner pup 
 or Handler. Then you’ll get to try out what you learned with an open rom
 p area for play and activities like “Trainer Says” and an obstacle cou
 rse to inspire your inner animal! Expect a large matted area alongside tea
 \, snacks\, and cocktails for purchase as you watch classes and socialize.
  There will be plenty of seating for lounging\, too! All human pets and Ha
 ndlers are welcome\, but please attend with respect that this space is que
 er and trans/gnc-centric. If you identify as Trans/GNC or BIPOC and are in
  need of financial assistance to attend\, please contact us at wileyxwolfe
 @protonmail.com or emckeown737@gmail.com\; or alternatively @quemu73 on In
 stagram for a discount code! EVENT SCHEDULE 12:00pm - Doors open 12:30-1:3
 0pm: “Finding Your Pup or Handler Identity” Class 1:40-2:40pm: “Spea
 k! Picking Your Personal Pup Voice” Class 2:45-3pm: Intro to Pup Romp Et
 iquette 3-5pm: Open Play Pup Romp and Activities! 5pm: Event End CLASSES 
 “Finding Your Pup or Handler Identity” with Wiley WolfeCurious about p
 up play but don’t know where you fit? Want to better understand your per
 sona? This class is designed to help you navigate the basics and find what
  best fits you. We’ll discuss pup play terms\, common archetypes\, how t
 o tune into your headspace\, subverting (or queering) expectations\, and m
 ore! You don’t need expensive gear or a partner to start exploring.“Sp
 eak! Picking Your Personal Pup Voice” with Ellie McKeown Are you just ex
 ploring pup play for the first time? Have you been a pup for awhile but do
 n&#x27\;t have a good idea about how to vocalize? This class will explore 
 how your barks\, whines and growls actually work\, as well as how you can 
 find your own voice as a petplayer. You&#x27\;ll learn about the different
  things that other petplayers use their vocalizations to communicate\, the
  systems that let that communication happen\, and ways they interact with 
 who you are so you can express yourself as a human pet in a way that feels
  distinctly you! EDUCATORS Wiley Wolfe (they/them) is a Handler\, genderqu
 eer leatherdyke and kink coach with 9+ years experience\, currently pursui
 ng a Masters’ equivalent certification in sexology. They are the founder
  of the online Wolfe Academy of Desire for kink education\, the co-founder
  of LA pet play group SoCal Creatures\, and the proud Owner of 2 human pup
 s. Their workshops have been sought across the US and Canada including Kin
 kfest\, Westcoast Bound\, and Dark Odyssey.They delight in guiding both ne
 w and experienced players on their journeys\, with a particular focus on s
 elf-exploration\, deepening intention\, and gender-fucked joy. Ellie McKeo
 wn (She/they) also known as Pup Thistle\, is a transfemme pup player and s
 ubmissive who is currently a graduate student at York University in Lingui
 stics. Her research focuses on the sociological side of language use in qu
 eer communities\, including pup players and people in the Japanese transfe
 minine cruising scene. This workshop draws on her MA research in non-human
  vocalizations as a communicative genre among pup players. (FOR MORE INFO 
 SEE TICKET LINK PROVIDED)
LOCATION:Bampot\, 201 Harbord St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/how-to-dog-a-human-pup-educational-and-pla
 y-event
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
